ticket extends with `low-disk`, but it is not listed in File impact (only docs/review-policy.md is named).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdcc98d5c4ca5749e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'File impact' section; consumer at src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md:176 (and the retryable-set prose in the same guide)","norm_id":"n4a2e4581efb762fb","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A contributor consulting passing-code-review.md after a low-disk deferral finds the sub-reason list does not mention low-disk, so the documented vocabulary is incomplete/inaccurate"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In File impact, add `src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md` alongside docs/review-policy.md and update its coverage-gap sub-reason list to include low-disk.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the intended terminal disposition of a low-disk deferral when the ADR 0069 retry budget is exhausted (e.g. keep deferring vote-less rather than escalating to the fail-closed -1 that other retryable reasons cast), and reflect it in an acceptance criterion.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["voter.py _handle_retryable_gap: at budget exhaustion calls append_retries_exhausted_note + _voter_error with vote_value=cfg.llm_review_block_value — i.e. a fail-closed -1","Ticket summary: goal is that review-bot must 'not post a vote while budget remains' but the exhaustion path is unspecified for low-disk","Part B says low-disk 'must not post a vote while budget remains' — silent on the after-budget case"],"finding":"The plan routes low-disk admission refusal through ADR 0069's _handle_retryable_gap, but does not state the intended TERMINAL disposition when the per-revision retry budget is exhausted. That funnel's exhaustion branch casts the fail-closed -1 (cfg.llm_review_block_value) and fires VOTER_ERROR — which would re-introduce the very fail-closed -1 this ticket exists to prevent, merely deferred by N attempts, for an infra condition unrelated to the change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1f177d9b2108284c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approved design → Part B ('route it through ADR 0069's existing _handle_retryable_gap bounded deferral')","norm_id":"nc0653f02d40bb653","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Sustained disk pressure that outlasts retryable_gap_max_attempts reconcile cycles — the change would still receive a fail-closed -1 for an infra condition it cannot influence"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the terminal disposition for a low-disk gap when the ADR 0069 deferral budget is exhausted (hold vote-less vs. post a vote), and confirm it does not fall through to the fail-closed -1 that the prior incident exhibited.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'must not post a vote while budget remains' — states the pre-exhaustion disposition but not the post-exhaustion (budget-exhausted) disposition","Summary: 'Change 2481 exhausted its retry budget to a fail-closed LLM-Review -1' — the terminal arm is exactly where the prior escape occurred","The low-disk arm is a newly-added retryable disposition; its budget-exhausted terminal leg is the disposition-contract gap"],"finding":"The plan alters disposition/retry semantics by adding low-disk to RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS and routing it through ADR 0069 bounded deferral as retryable/vote-less, but it does not state the TERMINAL disposition when the bounded deferral budget is exhausted for a low-disk gap. The prior incident (change 2481) 'exhausted its retry budget to a fail-closed LLM-Review -1' — the same escape this ticket targets. If low-disk deferral, once budget-exhausted, falls through to a fail-closed -1, the fix reintroduces the very defect class it closes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbff034f14ceb1197","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approved design — Part B; 'route it through ADR 0069's existing _handle_retryable_gap bounded deferral' / 'must not post a vote while budget remains'","norm_id":"n965492f918362891","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an explicit clause: on low-disk budget exhaustion the bot holds without posting a fail-closed -1 (or emits an operator alert instead of a review veto), and add a test asserting the budget-exhausted low-disk path does not post a coverage-gap/-1 vote.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the full shape of the synthesized low-disk decision (gap_reason, decision/BLOCK, and a message beginning with the [LLM-Review: BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)] tag) so it flows correctly through _handle_retryable_gap and classify_tag.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["adapter.append_retries_exhausted_note builds out['message'] from decision.get('message','') — an empty/absent message yields a degraded body","classify_tag / _GAP_RE parse the first-line tag; a synthesized decision without a properly-tagged message would classify as 'unparseable'"],"finding":"The plan specifies synthesizing a decision carrying gap_reason=\"low-disk\" and routing it through _handle_retryable_gap, but does not specify the synthesized decision dict's other required fields — notably a 'message' (append_retries_exhausted_note reads decision.get('message')) and the first-line [LLM-Review: BLOCK — coverage-gap (low-disk)] tag that the retrigger/classification and operator-facing vocabulary depend on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd5bc04cb9337fdd8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approved design → Part B ('synthesize a decision carrying gap_reason=low-disk')","norm_id":"n8d7f243f867a8d75","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Budget exhaustion on a low-disk decision that carried no message/tag — the posted -1 body and its retrigger classification would be malformed"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Note the empirical basis for the 2 GiB REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB floor (or a fixture measuring peak clone+materialization footprint), so the admission floor is derived from observed usage rather than asserted.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6933,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB (default 2 GiB ... a hard pre-clone admission floor'","Evidence section shows large non-cache consumers (Containers 3.572 GB) that a clone must coexist with","Prior escapes: 2731-4c53, 7a41-95f4, 3a52-2d79, 9bc0-1200, 28f9-535c, e2c5-f09b"],"finding":"The REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB default of 2 GiB is asserted rather than derived from observed clone/materialization footprint, despite this being a repeat escape of the fail-closed-on-full-disk class (six prior closed tickets). If a review clone plus snapshot materialization can transiently exceed 2 GiB, admission control could pass and still ENOSPC.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff5ee58e51079a6b9","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Part B — near-full review admission control; AC lines 3-4","norm_id":"ne9d8f31409f2e17f","priority":0.2567,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A large change materializes a clone whose peak working-set exceeds the 2 GiB free headroom, ENOSPC recurs despite passing admission control"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a brief rationale (or a measurement fixture) tying the 2 GiB default to the observed peak disk delta of a representative review clone + attested snapshot materialization.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Address the check-then-act race on the shared target volume: state whether concurrent clones are serialized/bounded or set REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB headroom to absorb worst-case concurrent clone size, and note expected concurrency on the rev